<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Sabvest half yr headline shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Sabvest half yr headline shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline			11.4  vs  3.0</p>
<p>    - attrib			  14.3  vs  8.3</p>
<p>    Attrib income		    7.38 vs  1.60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			    7.38 vs  4.29</p>
<p>    Tax				  --   vs   --</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    2.26 vs  4.64</p>
<p>    Operation/investment income 10.49 vs  8.63</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	   9.53 vs  7.52</p>
<p>Full name: Sabvest Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The investment holding company said the businesses in which the group has investments were performing satisfactorily and it expected headline earnings and dividends of 28-33 cents and five cents per share respectively for the 1997 financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
